  "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
  "label": "LGBTQ+ individuals are mapped onto the scene of state violence",
  "description": "The text 'go be gay somewhere else' explicitly targets LGBTQ+ individuals, and by juxtaposing this text with the visual of riot police using water cannons against protesters, the meme maps the concept of LGBTQ+ people onto the violent, exclusionary context depicted. The riot police and their violent actions are used as a visual metaphor for the hostile environment the text implies LGBTQ+ people should leave. This mapping is based on the hateful intent to associate being gay with the violent confrontation shown, thereby dehumanizing and marginalizing the group.",
